      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Tyseley railway station once served as a major junction for the Great Western Railway mainline between Birmingham Snow Hill and London Paddington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyseley",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Tyseley Locomotive Works, founded in the 19th century, still operates today restoring and maintaining steam locomotives.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/West_Midlands/Tyseley.html",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Tyseley’s industrial heritage is marked by long‑standing factories and warehouses that remain in use today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/West_Midlands/Tyseley.html",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area lies close to the Grand Union Canal, a historic waterway that once powered local industry.",
